; A global bound to a container is not representable in the term/proof encoding:
; a global's own row has no rebuild, so a container holding e-classes would go
; stale as the e-graph merges. So this file must be reported as not supporting
; proofs — a global bound to a primitive, by contrast, now is.
;
; The binding is wrapped in `(fail …)`, so the shared table it writes to is
; declared from inside the `fail`. Global removal hoists that declaration out,
; which is what lets the write still be recognized as a global one.
(datatype Math (Num i64))
(sort MathVec (Vec Math))

(fail (let $bad (vec-of (Num 1) (Num (/ 1 0)))))

(let $v (vec-of (Num 1) (Num 2)))
(check (= $v (vec-of (Num 1) (Num 2))))
